## Environments

### Environment Concept

**Environment** = grouping of nodes with specific configuration.

```
DEVELOPMENT
├─ Smaller resources
├─ Relaxed security
├─ Frequent changes
└─ Developers can modify

STAGING
├─ Similar to production
├─ Full testing
├─ Limited access
└─ Production-like behavior

PRODUCTION
├─ Maximum resources
├─ Strict security
├─ Careful changes
├─ High availability
```

**Environment Definition:**

```ruby
# environments/production.rb

name 'production'
description 'Production environment'

# Version locks for cookbooks
cookbook_versions(
  'apache2' => '= 3.1.0',
  'mysql' => '= 5.0.2',
  'php' => '= 2.0.0'
)

# Override attributes
override_attributes(
  'apache' => {
    'port' => 443,
    'ssl_enabled' => true
  },
  'mysql' => {
    'max_connections' => 5000,
    'slow_query_log' => true
  },
  'app' => {
    'debug' => false,
    'log_level' => 'warn'
  }
)
```

**Development Environment:**

```ruby
# environments/development.rb

name 'development'
description 'Development environment'

cookbook_versions(
  'apache2' => '~> 3.0',
  'mysql' => '~> 5.0'
)

override_attributes(
  'apache' => {
    'port' => 80,
    'ssl_enabled' => false
  },
  'mysql' => {
    'max_connections' => 100
  },
  'app' => {
    'debug' => true,
    'log_level' => 'debug'
  }
)
```

