## Knife Tool

### Knife Basics

**Knife** = Command-line tool for Chef management.

**Basic Commands:**

```bash
# Bootstrap a new node
knife bootstrap 192.168.1.100 \
  --ssh-user ubuntu \
  --sudo \
  --identity-file ~/.ssh/chef.pem \
  --node-name web1

# List all nodes
knife node list

# Show node details
knife node show web1

# Delete node
knife node delete web1

# Edit node
knife node edit web1
```

**Cookbook Management:**

```bash
# Create new cookbook
knife cookbook create my_cookbook

# Upload cookbook to Chef Server
knife cookbook upload my_cookbook

# Show cookbook details
knife cookbook show my_cookbook

# Download cookbook
knife cookbook download my_cookbook

# Delete cookbook
knife cookbook delete my_cookbook
```

**Role Management:**

```bash
# Create role
knife role create web_server

# Upload role
knife role from file roles/web_server.rb

# List roles
knife role list

# Show role
knife role show web_server

# Edit role
knife role edit web_server
```

**Environment Management:**

```bash
# Create environment
knife environment create production

# Upload environment
knife environment from file environments/production.rb

# List environments
knife environment list

# Show environment
knife environment show production
```

**Search:**

```bash
# Search nodes
knife search node "role:web_server"

# Search by attribute
knife search node "apache.port:80"

# Complex query
knife search node "role:web_server AND environment:production"
```

**SSH/Remote Execution:**

```bash
# SSH to node
knife ssh "name:web1" "uptime"

# Run command on all web servers
knife ssh "role:web_server" "tail -f /var/log/apache2/access.log"

# Execute on multiple nodes
knife ssh "environment:production" "chef-client"
```

