## Testing & Debugging

### Testing Approaches

**Types of Tests:**

```
UNIT TESTS (ChefSpec)
├─ Test recipe logic
├─ Fast execution
├─ No actual changes
└─ Uses mocked attributes

INTEGRATION TESTS (InSpec)
├─ Test actual system state
├─ Verify resources applied correctly
├─ Run on test nodes/VMs
└─ Comprehensive validation

SYNTAX CHECKS
├─ Validate Ruby syntax
├─ Check resource definitions
└─ Lint cookbooks
```

### ChefSpec (Unit Testing)

**Test Recipe Logic:**

```ruby
# spec/unit/recipes/default_spec.rb

require 'spec_helper'

describe 'my_cookbook::default' do
  platform 'ubuntu', '18.04'

  context 'When all attributes are default' do
    let(:chef_run) do
      ChefSpec::SoloRunner.new(platform: 'ubuntu', '18.04')
        .converge(described_recipe)
    end

    it 'converges successfully' do
      expect { chef_run }.not_to raise_error
    end

    it 'installs apache2' do
      expect(chef_run).to install_package('apache2')
    end

    it 'starts apache2 service' do
      expect(chef_run).to enable_service('apache2')
      expect(chef_run).to start_service('apache2')
    end

    it 'creates index.html' do
      expect(chef_run).to create_file('/var/www/html/index.html')
        .with(
          owner: 'www-data',
          group: 'www-data'
        )
    end
  end
end
```

**Run Tests:**

```bash
# Run all tests
chef exec rspec

# Run specific test
chef exec rspec spec/unit/recipes/default_spec.rb

# Run with debug output
chef exec rspec -v
```

### InSpec (Integration Testing)

**Verify System State:**

```ruby
# inspec/controls/default.rb

title 'Web Server Configuration'

# Check if Apache is installed
describe package('apache2') do
  it { should be_installed }
end

# Check if Apache service is running
describe service('apache2') do
  it { should be_installed }
  it { should be_enabled }
  it { should be_running }
end

# Check if port 80 is listening
describe port(80) do
  it { should be_listening }
  its('protocols') { should include 'tcp' }
end

# Check configuration file
describe file('/etc/apache2/apache2.conf') do
  it { should exist }
  its('owner') { should eq 'root' }
  its('group') { should eq 'root' }
  its('mode') { should cmp '0644' }
end

# Check content
describe file('/var/www/html/index.html') do
  its('content') { should match /Hello World/ }
end
```

**Run InSpec Tests:**

```bash
# Run locally on your machine
inspec exec inspec/

# Run on remote node
inspec exec inspec/ -t ssh://user@host

# Run with chef
chef exec inspec exec inspec/
```

### Debugging

**Logging:**

```ruby
# Print debug messages
log "Installing package: #{package_name}" do
  level :info
end

# Use ruby block for debugging
ruby_block 'debug_attributes' do
  block do
    Chef::Log.info("Apache port: #{node['apache']['port']}")
    Chef::Log.info("All attributes: #{node.to_hash}")
  end
end
```

**Chef Client Run with Debug:**

```bash
# Verbose output
chef-client -l debug

# Log file
chef-client -L /var/log/chef-client.log

# Only converge specific recipe
chef-client -o recipe[my_cookbook::default]

# Dry run (no changes)
chef-client --why-run

# Log to syslog
chef-client -L syslog
```

