## Best Practices

### Recipe Writing

**Do's:**

```ruby
# ✅ Use sensible defaults
default['app']['port'] = 8080

# ✅ Make recipes modular
# Split into separate recipes
recipe 'install'   # install packages
recipe 'configure' # configure files
recipe 'service'   # manage service

# ✅ Be explicit about actions
service 'apache2' do
  action [:enable, :start]
end

# ✅ Handle idempotence
file '/var/cache/app' do
  action :create_if_missing
end

# ✅ Use conditions
package 'apache2-mpm-prefork' do
  action :install
  not_if { node['apache']['mpm'] == 'worker' }
end

# ✅ Notify services of changes
template '/etc/apache2/apache2.conf' do
  notifies :restart, 'service[apache2]', :delayed
end

# ✅ Set proper ownership
file '/var/www/html/index.html' do
  owner 'www-data'
  group 'www-data'
  mode '0644'
end
```

**Don'ts:**

```ruby
# ❌ Hardcode values
port = 8080

# ❌ Use execute for everything
execute 'install-package' do
  command 'apt-get install apache2'
end

# ❌ Ignore service dependencies
package 'apache2'
template '/etc/apache2/apache2.conf' do
  action :create
end
# Missing: service restart

# ❌ Write brittle tests
expect(node['port']).to eq 8080

# ❌ Ignore platform differences
package 'httpd' # Works on CentOS, not Ubuntu

# ❌ Make recipes too complex
# Move business logic to libraries instead
```

### Organization

**Cookbook Structure:**

```
cookbooks/
├─ base/               # Common setup
│  ├─ recipes/
│  └─ attributes/
├─ apache/            # Web server
├─ mysql/             # Database
└─ application/       # Custom app

roles/
├─ web_server.rb
├─ database_server.rb
└─ cache_server.rb

environments/
├─ production.rb
├─ staging.rb
└─ development.rb
```

### Naming Conventions

```ruby
# Cookbooks: lowercase, hyphens
my-web-cookbook
apache-ssl-config

# Recipes: lowercase, underscores
recipes/default.rb
recipes/web_server.rb
recipes/database_setup.rb

# Attributes: descriptive paths
default['apache']['port']
default['database']['host']

# Resources: lowercase, underscores
package 'apache2'
service 'mysql'
user 'appuser'
```

