## Testing & Debugging

### Q13: How do you test Chef cookbooks? Explain ChefSpec and InSpec

**Answer:**

ChefSpec provides unit testing (what will the recipe do?). InSpec provides integration testing (does the system actually work?).

**Theory:**

```
TESTING PYRAMID:

         Acceptance
           (Manual)
        ↑
       /  \
      /    \
    Integration
    (InSpec)
    ↑
   /  \
  /    \
Unit Tests
(ChefSpec)

Speed:    ChefSpec (fast) → InSpec (medium) → Acceptance (slow)
Coverage: ChefSpec (low) → InSpec (high) → Acceptance (actual)
```

**ChefSpec (Unit Testing):**

```ruby
# spec/spec_helper.rb
require 'chefspec'

ChefSpec::SoloRunner.new do |node|
  # Set attributes for testing
  node.automatic['os'] = 'linux'
end.converge described_recipe

# spec/unit/recipes/default_spec.rb
require 'spec_helper'

describe 'apache::default' do
  platform 'ubuntu', '18.04'
  
  let(:chef_run) do
    ChefSpec::ServerRunner.new(platform: 'ubuntu', version: '18.04') do |node|
      node.automatic['memory']['total'] = '2GB'
    end.converge(described_recipe)
  end
  
  it 'installs apache2 package' do
    expect(chef_run).to install_package('apache2')
  end
  
  it 'creates apache configuration file' do
    expect(chef_run).to create_template('/etc/apache2/apache2.conf')
  end
  
  it 'enables and starts apache service' do
    expect(chef_run).to enable_service('apache2')
    expect(chef_run).to start_service('apache2')
  end
  
  it 'notifies service restart when config changes' do
    expect(chef_run.template('/etc/apache2/apache2.conf'))
      .to notify('service[apache2]').to(:restart).delayed
  end
end
```

**Running ChefSpec:**

```bash
# Run all tests
chef exec rspec

# Run specific test
chef exec rspec spec/unit/recipes/default_spec.rb

# Run with detailed output
chef exec rspec -f documentation
```

**InSpec (Integration Testing):**

```ruby
# test/integration/default/apache_spec.rb
describe 'Apache Installation' do
  it 'installs apache2 package' do
    expect(package('apache2')).to be_installed
  end
  
  it 'starts apache service' do
    expect(service('apache2')).to be_running
    expect(service('apache2')).to be_enabled
  end
  
  it 'listens on port 80' do
    expect(port(80)).to be_listening
    expect(port(80)).to be_listening.with('tcp')
  end
  
  it 'serves content' do
    expect(http('http://localhost')).to be_responding
    expect(http('http://localhost')).to have_status(200)
  end
  
  it 'has correct configuration' do
    expect(file('/etc/apache2/apache2.conf')).to exist
    expect(file('/etc/apache2/apache2.conf')).to be_file
    expect(file('/etc/apache2/apache2.conf')).to have_mode('0644')
  end
  
  it 'has correct permissions' do
    expect(file('/var/www/html')).to be_directory
    expect(file('/var/www/html')).to be_owned_by('root')
  end
  
  it 'loads required modules' do
    expect(apache_conf('/etc/apache2/mods-enabled/rewrite.load')).to exist
  end
end
```

**Running InSpec:**

```bash
# Run InSpec tests
inspec exec test/integration/default

# Run with specific profile
inspec exec test/integration/default --controls apache

# Run against remote node
inspec exec . -t ssh://ubuntu@192.168.1.100 -i ~/.ssh/key.pem

# Generate report
inspec exec . --reporter json > report.json
```

**Test Kitchen (Local Testing):**

```yaml
# .kitchen.yml
---
driver:
  name: vagrant

provisioner:
  name: chef_zero
  product_name: chef

platforms:
  - name: ubuntu-18.04
  - name: centos-7

suites:
  - name: default
    run_list:
      - recipe[apache::default]
    verifier:
      inspec_tests:
        - test/integration/default
```

**Test Kitchen Commands:**

```bash
# Create test instance
kitchen create

# Run converge (apply recipe)
kitchen converge

# Run tests
kitchen verify

# Destroy instance
kitchen destroy

# All in one
kitchen test
```

**Key Points:**
- ✅ ChefSpec = Unit tests (fast, mock)
- ✅ InSpec = Integration tests (slow, real)
- ✅ Test Kitchen = Local testing environment
- ✅ Write tests before recipes (TDD)
- ✅ Automated testing prevents regressions

