### Q14: How do you debug Chef runs?

**Answer:**

Use Chef's logging, why-run mode, and detailed output to debug configuration issues.

**Debugging Methods:**

```bash
# 1. RUN WITH DEBUG LOGGING
chef-client -l debug

# 2. WHY-RUN MODE (Show what would happen without applying)
chef-client --why-run

# 3. SINGLE RUN WITH SPECIFIC RECIPE
chef-client -o recipe[cookbook::recipe] -l debug

# 4. DRY-RUN (Simulate without making changes)
chef-client -W

# 5. NODE ATTRIBUTE OUTPUT
chef-client -o recipe[debug::show_attributes]
```

**In Recipes:**

```ruby
# recipes/debug.rb

# Log attribute values
Chef::Log.info("Current port: #{node['app']['port']}")

# Conditional logging
Chef::Log.warn("Debug mode enabled!") if node['app']['debug']

# Ruby block for debugging
ruby_block 'debug_info' do
  block do
    Chef::Log.info("Knife environment: #{node.environment}")
    Chef::Log.info("Node name: #{node.name}")
    Chef::Log.info("Run list: #{node.run_list}")
    puts JSON.pretty_generate(node['app'])
  end
end

# Show all attributes
ruby_block 'show_all_attributes' do
  block do
    Chef::Log.info JSON.pretty_generate(node.attributes)
  end
end

# Pause execution for investigation
ruby_block 'pause_for_debug' do
