## Real-World Scenarios

### Q17: Design a multi-tier application deployment

**Answer:**

```
ARCHITECTURE:

Load Balancer Tier
├─ 2x nginx (port 443, 80)

Web Application Tier
├─ 3x Node.js servers (port 8080)
├─ Session store (Redis)

Database Tier
├─ MySQL Master-Slave replication
├─ Automated backups

Monitoring Tier
├─ Prometheus (metrics)
├─ ELK Stack (logging)
```

**Chef Implementation:**

```ruby
# roles/load_balancer.rb
name 'load_balancer'
run_list(
  'recipe[nginx]',
  'recipe[nginx::ssl]',
  'recipe[monitoring::agent]'
)

# roles/web_server.rb
name 'web_server'
run_list(
  'recipe[nodejs]',
  'recipe[app-deploy]',
  'recipe[redis-client]',
  'recipe[monitoring::agent]'
)

# roles/database_server.rb
name 'database_server'
run_list(
  'recipe[mysql::server]',
  'recipe[mysql::replication]',
  'recipe[mysql::backup]',
  'recipe[monitoring::agent]'
)

# Deployment recipe
# recipes/app-deploy.rb
user 'appuser' do
  home '/home/appuser'
  shell '/bin/bash'
end

directory '/var/www/app' do
  owner 'appuser'
  group 'appuser'
  mode '0755'
  recursive true
end

git '/var/www/app' do
  repository 'https://github.com/myorg/app.git'
  revision node['app']['version']
  action :sync
  user 'appuser'
  group 'appuser'
  notifies :restart, 'service[app]'
end

execute 'install-dependencies' do
  command 'npm install'
  cwd '/var/www/app'
  user 'appuser'
  notifies :restart, 'service[app]'
end

systemd_unit 'app.service' do
  content({
    Unit: {
      Description: 'Node.js Application',
      After: 'network.target'
    },
    Service: {
      Type: 'simple',
      User: 'appuser',
      WorkingDirectory: '/var/www/app',
      ExecStart: '/usr/bin/node /var/www/app/index.js',
      Restart: 'always'
    },
    Install: {
      WantedBy: 'multi-user.target'
    }
  })
  action [:create, :enable, :start]
end

service 'app' do
  action :nothing
end
```

